WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.680
What is Python? Python is a general-purpose&nbsp;
language with a wide variety of uses, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:16.000
for basic apps, web development, data analysis,&nbsp;
artificial intelligence, the Internet of Things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.120
automation, and the topic we will use to teach&nbsp;
the concepts in this course: game development.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:29.640
Take a look at this example of Python code. Python&nbsp;
code is known for being more natural-looking than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:37.440
some other languages, namely Java, JavaScript,&nbsp;
and C#. We do not see curly brackets here as we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:44.280
do in other languages. However, and this will be&nbsp;
emphasized throughout the course, Python is big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:55.760
on indentation. For one example, notice the code&nbsp;
inside this if statement: it is indented. If the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:01.640
code is not indented properly, it will not work.&nbsp;
The more practice you get in recognizing when code&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:10.520
needs to be indented, the easier it will be to&nbsp;
determine when code needs to be indented. Python&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:17.320
is also an interpreted language, which means you&nbsp;
can write code and run it in the Python engine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:22.680
as opposed to a compiled language, such as C#,&nbsp;
which needs to be compiled into an executable or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:29.160
similar file before it can be run. We also do not&nbsp;
need to worry about memory management in Python as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:35.880
in other programming languages. Python is one&nbsp;
of many object-oriented programming languages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:42.360
in that classes can be created, and objects can be&nbsp;
built within those classes. Classes are beyond the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:51.160
scope of this exam, but know that they do exist.&nbsp;
Python is also a dynamically typed language,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:59.240
meaning that data types do not need to be declared&nbsp;
on variables before the variables themselves are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:05.680
declared. While on the subject of data types,&nbsp;
operations with data types and operators is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:12.400
the first exam objective set in this course, so&nbsp;
let’s learn about those data types and operators.

